Task 1: Install JDK
Install JDK 11 or higher on your system.

Set the JAVA_HOME environment variable.

Verify installation:

Run java -version → should display installed version.

Run echo %JAVA_HOME% (Windows) or echo $JAVA_HOME (Mac/Linux) → should display JDK path.


Task 2: Install Android Studio & SDKs
Download and install Android Studio.

Open SDK Manager inside Android Studio.

Install the latest Android SDK Platform and Android SDK Tools.

Take a screenshot of the installed SDKs in SDK Manager.


Task 3: Create Android Virtual Device (AVD)
Open AVD Manager in Android Studio.

Create a new AVD with a profile similar to your phone (e.g., Pixel 4, Android 11).

Launch the emulator and show the home screen.

Capture a screenshot of the emulator running.


Task 4: Connect Real Android Device
Enable USB debugging on your Android device (Developer Options → USB Debugging).

Connect your device via USB.

Run adb devices in terminal → confirm your device is detected.

If device is not detected, install the required drivers.

Capture a screenshot of the terminal showing your device listed.


Task 5: Install Node.js & Appium
Install Node.js v14 or above.

Verify installation:

Run node -v and npm -v.

Install Appium globally:

bash
npm install -g appium
Start Appium server:

bash
appium
Capture terminal output showing Appium server running and listening on port 4723.


